# Execution router

The one rule that decides **what to load and whether to act**. Runs before responding to the first user message in any conversation, including resumes.

## 0. Workspace detection and default agent

The BA Assistant orchestrator is the **default agent** in any workspace containing `.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/` or an initiative folder, or set up per SETUP.md. The user does not type `/ba-assistant` — classify the turn and engage silently when BA-related. Outside BA workspaces, never auto-engage.

## 1. Project context (first chat in a workspace)

Read the workspace root's `AGENTS.md` as primary context, else `README.md`. Do not assume a specific product. Load BA skills **only** from `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/` (or this package's `skills/ba-assistant/` when installing); never search other skill folders.

## 2. Classify the turn (first action, silent)

| Class | Signals | Required reads (Read tool) | Then |
|-------|---------|---------------------------|------|
| **BA-resume** | continue, resume, #2, initiative name, `/next` `/status` | `SKILL.md` Step 2 read order (snapshot first) | Run `SKILL.md` Step 2 (resume / `/reanchor`). **Act on the recommended next action**, do not status-dump only. No welcome panel. |
| **BA-new** | new initiative, Phase 0, intake | `instructions.md` only | Run `ba-new-initiative`, then `SKILL.md` Step 3 (Intake Reviewer). No welcome panel, no draft-depth quiz, no automatic canvas. |
| **Publish-risk** | hand to devs, publish to the team/delivery repo, push analysis to a shared repo, `/handover` | Route via `skills-routing.mdc` to `ba-dev-handover` | Publish confirmed analysis only. **No write/push until the user explicitly says to** (see Publish guard below). Plain "sync" is not this class: it means `/wrap`, Jira/Confluence status (`ba-jira-sync`, `/publish-status`), or `/validate-state`. Ask once if unclear. |
| **BA-tooling** | improve BA assistant, new skill/sub-skill/rule/command/hook, workboard package, "for another BA", change routing/orchestrator, edit `ba-assistant-cursor-skill` skills/rules/commands | Your local-first packaging rule, if you have one | **Edit `~/.cursor/` first.** No writes to the package repo's skills/rules/commands/hooks until the local change exists and the BA has confirmed it. |
| **Non-BA** | debug code, syntax, generic explain | Project README/AGENTS only | Skip BA orchestrator |
| **Ambiguous** | "help me think through something", short message either way | — | Ask once via AskQuestion: BA Assistant (recommended) / Quick chat / Specific skill. "Quick chat" = orchestrator stays off for the thread. |
| **Chat checkpoint** | wrap up, close out this chat, checkpoint, `/wrap` | `~/.cursor/commands/wrap.md` | Run `/wrap`: chat-only checkpoint into `SESSION-CONTEXT.md` and the tracker. Not a retro, not end of day. |
| **End of day** | done for tonight, end of day, `/EOD`, `/eod`, `/workboard end-of-day` | `commands/eod.md` | Full closeout per `eod-closeout-procedure.md`. No retrospective. |
| **Retro** | `/retro`, or the user explicitly asks for a retro / retrospective / lessons learned | `SESSION-CONTEXT.md` (tail) | Load **ba-retrospective-and-learning**: Type 1 default; Type 2 if tooling/process failure this session. Only on explicit request. |

Also classify the **activity** (Frame / Discover / Shape / Deliver / Run — see `references/activity-map.md`). Do not print model-tier nudges (Auto-balance handles model selection).

### Publish guard (publish-risk)

1. Publishing to devs goes through `ba-dev-handover` only. It never publishes unconfirmed work.
2. Do not write or push to a shared repo until the user explicitly says to.
3. No bulk copy of working notes (`Copy-Item -Recurse`, whole-folder copies) to a shared or team repo. Publish selected confirmed artefacts file by file with review.
4. When a shared-repo path is configured (`paths.sharedRepoRoot` in `ba-assistant-config.mdc`, or `BA_SHARED_REPO_ROOT`), the shared-repo guard hook still applies on commit/push.

### Mid-thread opt-out

"Skip the BA assistant", "just answer my question", "no orchestrator", "drop out of BA Assistant" → suspend the orchestrator for the rest of the thread, acknowledge briefly. Re-engage only on explicit "run BA assistant" / "back to BA Assistant".

### Mid-thread re-anchor

`/reanchor` follows `~/.cursor/commands/reanchor.md`. The Anti-Pattern Detector flags drift and offers it proactively.

## 2b. Use the BA's settings (`ba-assistant-config.mdc`)

`/setup` writes `~/.cursor/rules/ba-assistant-config.mdc` (always in context). Use its values everywhere instead of package placeholders, and never ask for one that is set: `[BA name]` → `name` (plus `role`, `team`); Jira → `jira.instanceUrl`, `jira.projectKey`; Confluence → `confluence.spaceKey`, `confluence.parentPageUrl`; domain → `domain`, `domainDocs` (shape questions, research and examples); folders → `paths.initiativesRoot`, `paths.downloadsPath`, `paths.sharedRepoRoot`. An initiative's `status-data.json` / `confluence-pages.json` overrides Jira and Confluence values; an upper-case env var (`BA_INITIATIVES_ROOT` etc.) overrides the config. A value still in `[brackets]` counts as unset: ask once, then offer to save it. `PROJ-1234` keys in package examples are illustrations.

## 3. Skill loading — one primary, not bulk

**Bootstrap (BA only):** per `ba-assistant/SKILL.md` Step 1.

**Routing:** on a BA or matched intent, **Read** `skills-routing.mdc` (agent-requested; not always injected). Load **one primary** skill for the turn. Load a **second** only when intents are clearly complementary (e.g. workshop design + Miro board analysis). Prefer the more specific row on conflicts. **Never** read all BA sub-skills before the first reply. **Never** skip `SKILL.md` Step 2 file reads on a resume thread.

**Report loads inline:** every skill load/invocation gets a one-line header — `> **Skill loaded:** [name] — [reason]`. Skip for internal tool calls.

## 4. Continuous monitors (every BA turn, silent unless triggered)

### Anti-Pattern Detector (quick scan)

After any BA output, self-check against the top triggers. If one fires, load `ba-anti-pattern-detector` for the full rule set and surface an inline warning. Otherwise proceed silently.

| # | Check | Pattern |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Premature solutioning | Solution proposed without confirmed requirements |
| 2 | Missing interrogation | Requirement/decision accepted unchallenged |
| 3 | Skipped slicing | Epics/stories without feature slices |
| 4 | Scope creep unlogged | Scope changed, no SESSION-CONTEXT entry |
| 5 | Thread drift | >20 turns AND topic shifted from opening intent |
| 6 | Long session unsynced | >20 turns regardless of topic — the stop-hook sync check will also flag unpromoted items |

### Context Capture (passive)

After every user message in a BA thread, scan for decisions, requirements, actions, answered questions, assumptions, risks, blockers, facts and corrections. When something is found, write it the same turn with one `_workstream/capture.py` call (`--source chat-user` for what the BA said, else the real source) and add a `📝 Captured:` line (per `ba-context-capture`). Nothing found: stay silent, write nothing. Debriefing a transcript or pasted document: skip this, its items go on the debrief card.

### Skill nudges (content-aware routing)

| Signal | Consider loading |
|---|---|
| "requirement", "acceptance criteria", "AC" | ba-requirements-interrogator |
| "option A/B", "trade-off", "solution design" | ba-solution-shaping |
| "stakeholder", "RACI", "who owns/decides" | ba-stakeholder-strategy |
| "change management", "adoption", "rollout comms" | ba-change-strategy |
| "current state", "as-is", "how does it work today" | ba-current-state-assessment |
| "playback", "sign-off", "presentation to" | ba-playback-and-enablement |
| "hand to devs", "spike request", "ADR request" | ba-dev-handover |

## 5. Report (one line)

> **Session context:** [class] | Activity: [activity] | Skills: [loaded] | BA: [active/skipped]

## 6. Required visible outputs (BA-resume reply) — the Re-entry Card

On a BA-resume reply, read `~/.cursor/skills/ba-assistant/references/re-entry-card.md` and show that card (one screen: where we are, next action, today's meetings, new transcripts, Jira age, sync status), then AskQuestion with the recommended next action first. "Resume" with no initiative named: the cross-initiative mini-workboard in the same file. Non-negotiables: read state files before the card (never from memory), always include the next action, always include the AskQuestion, no Jira query.
